Where the files in this directory come from

Each file is an answer from the Web API of SonarQube Community Build 26.11.0.134175 (the
sonarqube:community image, sha256:7b2296713a92b8ea0dd7a083a25faadc59376c9a1e6daf2744a89711c54ea1ba),
recorded on 2026-11-26 after SonarScanner CLI analyzed a three-file Python repository written for
these tests. The repository's one source file, app/client.py, turns certificate checks off, reads a
JWT without checking its signature and asks for TLS 1.0. One of the four issues was then accepted in
SonarQube, with a comment.

project_analyses.json  /api/project_analyses/search?project=draugr-fixture&ps=1
issues.json            /api/issues/search, with the parameters Draugr sends
rules-python-*.json    /api/rules/show?key=python:<rule>

The rule answers keep only the fields Draugr reads. Each rule's description (descriptionSections and
educationPrinciples) is SonarSource's text, and is left out. SonarQube's random ids for issues,
analyses, events and comments are replaced with short names such as issue-S4423, because a secret
scanner reads a random value beside "key" as a credential. Nothing else is changed.
